/**
 * expect: JD-F01 (against f2_requirement.jd)
 * The leaf e_grid asserts what f2_requirement.jd proves with a whole argument, and says so
 * itself: the trailing (R22) tag names the requirement that makes it true. The corpus
 * contains the proof and this model declines to use it.
 *
 * The fix is to refine against it, storing the refine here under the reused name:
 *     load "f2_requirement.jd"
 *     justification consumer_base { ... }
 *     justification consumer is refine(consumer_base, r22) { hook: "e_grid" }
 *
 * Delete f2_requirement.jd from the corpus and this must become an OPEN QUESTION, not a
 * finding: the tag alone says a requirement exists, not that anyone argued it. That is the
 * pair case, and it is the difference between this rule and jpipe-review's C01.
 */
justification consumer {
    conclusion c is "The decision table is exhaustive over the input domain"
    strategy   s is "Confront the table's row count with the size of the input domain; every combination has a row"
    evidence   e_grid is "The identity grid is the full 27-cell one (R22)"

    s supports c
    e_grid supports s
}
